<BaseLayout title="Phone Lights and Confetti — Huanyu Chen"
  description="Five years of live music and shows, October 2021 to October 2026: radio festivals at the Hollywood Bowl, four nights at the Kia Forum, Taylor Swift's Eras Tour opening night in LA, a Genshin Impact symphony, Lang Lang playing Beethoven, and Bruno Mars twice.">
  <p class="muted"><a href="/misc">← Misc</a> · 2021–2026</p>
  <h1>Phone Lights and Confetti</h1>
  <p class="muted trip-sub">Five years of concerts and shows, in the order they happened.</p>

  <div class="callout trip-stats">
    <strong>24 shows · 15 venues · October 2021 – October 2026</strong><br />
    2 radio festivals at the Hollywood Bowl · 4 nights at the Kia Forum · 3 stadium shows at SoFi · 2 at Banc of California Stadium · 3 orchestras ·
    6 shows in Las Vegas<br />
    Seen twice: Imagine Dragons and Bruno Mars · most visited: the Kia Forum · cameras not allowed: Kenshi Yonezu
  </div>

  <p>
    When I went through five years of photos for the other posts on this page, one kind of evening kept turning up:
    a dark room, a bright stage far away, and a few minutes of shaky video. There are more of them than I expected.
    Some were big nights we planned for months. Others were tickets bought the same week, or a show added to a trip
    because we happened to be in town.
  </p>
  <p>
    This post puts them in order, from Maroon 5 at a soccer stadium in October 2021 to a
    stadium show at SoFi in October 2026. Each section says what the photos show, which is not always the same as
    what the ticket said. The first few, up to the summer of 2022, I went to by myself or with friends. From then on,
    "we" means the two of us. The Las Vegas shows already have their own posts, so they only get a short paragraph
    and a link here.
  </p>

  <h2>2021</h2>

  <h3 id="maroon5-2021">Maroon 5 · Banc of California Stadium · October 2, 2021</h3>
  <p>
    The first concert in this collection. Maroon 5's 2021 tour came to <strong>Banc of California
    Stadium</strong>, the soccer stadium next to the Coliseum in Exposition Park. It opened in 2018 for the LAFC
    soccer club and was renamed BMO Stadium in 2023. The screens inside listed blackbear and Ava Max as special
    guests, and next to them was a reminder of that autumn: everyone over the age of two had to stay masked,
    vaccinated or not. I went with friends. We were in our seats by seven, while the sky was still light and an
    opening act was on the side screens.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'maroon5-sign.webp'} alt="A screen announcing Maroon 5's 2021 tour with special guests blackbear and Ava Max, Saturday, October 2, at Banc of California." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The bill on the screens inside, 6:54 pm.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'maroon5-dusk.webp'} alt="A soccer stadium at dusk, its curved white roof lit from below, with a stage and two screens at the far end and people still finding their seats on the floor." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Still filling up at 7:01 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    Most of the videos are from the main set, from eight o'clock on. The stage was dressed like a garden, with
    potted palms, a painted backdrop and a white arch, under a huge rig of lights and speakers. The last photos, at
    10:52, are of the crowd heading out.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'maroon5-stage.webp'} alt="A concert stage under a tall steel rig of lights and speakers, with potted palms, a painted backdrop and a white arch, and a seated crowd in front." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The stage at 9:17 pm.</figcaption></figure>

  <h3 id="wcs-2021">We Can Survive · Hollywood Bowl · October 23, 2021</h3>
  <p>
    Three weeks later came the Hollywood Bowl. <em>We Can Survive</em> is
    an annual charity concert put on by the radio company Audacy, with several big acts on one bill. In 2021 it
    was at the <strong>Hollywood Bowl</strong>, which opened in 1922 in a natural hollow in the hills, under the
    white concentric arches of its shell. I went with friends. We came up the hill through the crowd at six, and by
    6:34, when it was nearly dark, the shell was lit red around a big round screen.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'wcs-2021-bowl.webp'} alt="The Hollywood Bowl's white arched shell lit red at dusk, with a large round screen and lighting rigs inside it, and the audience in the dark below." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The Bowl at dusk, 6:34 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    The headliner was Coldplay. The videos from the last part of the night show the whole amphitheater glowing
    with small lights: LED wristbands, which Coldplay's shows hand out and switch on together, so the seats change
    color with the music. At one point the shell itself was covered in handwritten Korean: 너는 내 별이자 내 우주, "you are my star and my universe." That is
    a line from "My Universe," the Coldplay and BTS single that had come out a month before.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'wcs-2021-my-universe.webp'} alt="The Hollywood Bowl shell washed in purple light, with handwritten Korean words projected across its top arch, the band small on the stage and side screens showing the singer." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>A line from "My Universe" written across the shell.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    The set ended with "A Sky Full of Stars." Forty minutes into my last video, fireworks went up from behind the
    shell, gold first and then pink, over the trees on the hill, while the seats below kept glowing with wristbands.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'wcs-2021-fireworks.webp'} alt="Pink and gold fireworks bursting over the Hollywood Bowl at night, smoke drifting over the dark trees, the shell lit purple below and the audience glowing with small lights." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>"A Sky Full of Stars," 10:20 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    It stayed with me. By the next afternoon I had painted it: the gold shell, the dark green hill, the rows of
    seats, and the sky above it full of red, pink and gold bursts.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig narrow-fig"><img src={P + 'wcs-2021-painting.webp'} alt="A painting of the Hollywood Bowl: a gold shell with a red and pink stage inside, rows of seats in red, gold and green below, a dark green hill behind, and bursts of red, pink and gold fireworks in the sky." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The painting, October 24, 2021.</figcaption></figure>

  <h2>2022</h2>

  <h3 id="alter-ego-2022">ALTer EGO · Kia Forum · January 15, 2022</h3>
  <p>
    Three months later came the first of four nights at the <strong>Kia Forum</strong> in Inglewood. The Forum
    opened in 1967 and was the Lakers' home until 1999. From the outside it is a round, colonnaded drum, and that night
    it was lit pink. Inside, the event was iHeartRadio's <em>ALTer EGO</em>, a one-night alternative-rock show with
    a long bill. The act the photos show most clearly is Måneskin. At 7:59 pm the screen said
    <strong>MÅNESKIN</strong> in white letters, between iHeartRadio logos, while beams of warm light fanned out
    under the ceiling of the Forum.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'alter-ego-maneskin.webp'} alt="The inside of the Kia Forum: a stage with a screen reading MÅNESKIN and iHeartRadio logos, beams of light fanning out under a ceiling dotted with small lights, and a packed arena." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Måneskin at ALTer EGO, 7:59 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    Måneskin are a rock band from Rome who had won the Eurovision Song Contest the previous May and were in the
    middle of a very fast rise. The rest of that night's bill included Coldplay, Imagine Dragons and twenty one
    pilots, and the phone kept recording until almost eleven. Looking back, it is a little funny how many of these
    names come back later in this post.
  </p>

  <h3>David Copperfield · MGM Grand, Las Vegas · March 13, 2022</h3>
  <p>
    The first show in Las Vegas was a magic show. On a desert road trip with friends, we came into the city from
    Death Valley and, after dinner, went to the MGM Grand to see <strong>David Copperfield</strong>, who has
    performed there for many years. There are no photos from inside. The story of that trip is in
    <a href="/misc/desert-2022">Death Valley, Vegas &amp; Page</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>The Stanford Philharmonia · Bing Concert Hall · May 21, 2022</h3>
  <p>
    On a Bay Area road trip with a friend, the afternoon at Stanford included the Stanford Philharmonia at
    <strong>Bing Concert Hall</strong>. Bing opened in 2013. It is a "vineyard" hall, with the seats in terraces all
    the way around the stage and big curved panels hanging overhead to shape the sound. The one photo shows the
    student orchestra on stage and the terraces behind it. There is more about that day in
    <a href="/misc/roadtrips-2022">Road Trips, 2022</a>.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'bing-concert-hall.webp'} alt="An orchestra seated on the stage of Bing Concert Hall, surrounded by terraced wooden seating under curving panels." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Bing Concert Hall, May 21, 2022.</figcaption></figure>

  <h3 id="zedd-2022">Zedd In The Park · Los Angeles State Historic Park · July 8, 2022</h3>
  <p>
    The summer of 2022 was the busiest stretch in this post: three shows in eight days. The first was outdoors, at
    <strong>Los Angeles State Historic Park</strong>, a long strip of lawn just north of Chinatown on what used to be
    a rail yard. <em>Zedd In The Park</em> was a one-day show built around the German producer Zedd. The set
    times, saved on the phone that afternoon, ran from doors at 5 pm to Zedd himself from 9:25
    to 11:00, after five other acts. At 7:54, in the last daylight, the photo is of the event's mascot: a white Z hanging inside a big
    steel ring.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'zedd-z.webp'} alt="A large white letter Z hanging inside a circular steel truss ring against an evening sky, with trees and hills behind." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The Z at Zedd In The Park, 7:54 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    After dark, the main stage turned into a wall of LED panels. During Zedd's set, the video at 10:02 shows the
    panels glowing orange and green lasers cutting through the smoke.
  </p>

  <h3 id="willow-avril-2022">WILLOW, Avril Lavigne and Machine Gun Kelly · Kia Forum · July 13, 2022</h3>
  <p>
    I have always filed this one under Avril Lavigne, but the photos tell a fuller story. It was a stop on Machine Gun Kelly's <em>Mainstream Sellout</em> tour, with Avril Lavigne and WILLOW opening. WILLOW
    was on first. At 8:09 her emblem, a W inside a flower-of-life pattern, hung over the stage in blue light, with a
    toy-like airplane prop up in the rig.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'willow-emblem.webp'} alt="A concert stage bathed in blue and teal light, with a large banner showing a W inside a circular flower-of-life pattern, and an airplane prop hanging above it." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>WILLOW's emblem, 8:09 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    Then, from about 8:40, a red curtain with <strong>Avril Lavigne</strong> written across it in a gothic script
    inside a heart, bunches of black balloons on either side, and Avril in front of it in yellow. She was touring
    her album <em>Love Sux</em>, released that February. The headliner came on later, and
    it was a different kind of show. At 9:52 the video catches Machine Gun Kelly, pink-haired, in a pastel suit,
    hanging off the side of a pink-and-black striped helicopter high above the floor. Near the end, the screen showed
    him on a checkerboard floor with a blonde singer beside him, who looks very much like Avril back for a duet.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'avril-curtain.webp'} alt="A band on stage in front of a large red curtain reading Avril Lavigne in gothic script inside a heart, with bunches of black balloons on each side." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Avril Lavigne, about 8:45 pm.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'mgk-helicopter.webp'} alt="A performer in a pastel suit hanging off a pink-and-black striped helicopter suspended high above the arena." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The headliner's entrance, 9:52 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h3 id="slander-2022">SLANDER · Long Beach Arena · July 15, 2022</h3>
  <p>
    Two nights later I was at the <strong>Long Beach Arena</strong> for SLANDER, an EDM duo from Los Angeles. The
    arena opened in 1962 next to the convention center and is better known from outside, for the giant whale mural
    that wraps around it. Inside, it was a dark, smoky room with a floor full of people. The best of the videos is
    from a little before ten: a DJ booth on a long riser and, behind it, a screen running anime-style animation, first a burst of
    light, then a pair of huge animated eyes.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'slander-anime.webp'} alt="A DJ booth on a riser in front of a huge LED screen showing an anime-style burst of orange and yellow light, with smoke and raised hands below." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The DJ riser at Long Beach Arena, 9:47 pm.</figcaption></figure>

  <h3 id="imagine-dragons-2022">Imagine Dragons · Banc of California Stadium · September 15, 2022</h3>
  <p>
    In September it was back to <strong>Banc of California Stadium</strong>, almost a year after Maroon 5, for
    Imagine Dragons on the <em>Mercury</em> World Tour. The videos show Dan Reynolds
    shirtless on a catwalk, a sea of phone lights in the stands, and two storms of confetti, one red and one gold,
    with big balloons bouncing over the floor. Afterwards the name was lit up in gold above the gates.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'imagine-confetti.webp'} alt="Gold confetti filling the air of a stadium under bright stage lights, with a large balloon bouncing above the crowd." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Confetti and balloons near the end, 10:50 pm.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'banc-of-california.webp'} alt="Gold letters reading BANC OF CALIFORNIA STADIUM along the curved steel canopy of a stadium at night." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>On the way out, 10:59 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h3 id="blackbear-2022">blackbear · YouTube Theater · September 26, 2022</h3>
  <p>
    Eleven days later we were in Inglewood for the singer and producer blackbear, who had been on the Maroon 5 bill a year earlier, at the <strong>YouTube
    Theater</strong>, a 6,000-seat hall that opened in 2021 beside SoFi Stadium. The opening act was the pop-punk band
    Waterparks, whose name glowed in pink neon on the stage. The screens beside the stage spent the changeover
    advertising a Smokey Robinson show in December. The best photo, though, is of the building before the show,
    its pale curved wall and the red YouTube logo almost the only color in it.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'youtube-theater.webp'} alt="The pale curved wall of the YouTube Theater at night, with a glowing YouTube Theater sign on a hedge and a row of steel bollards in front." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The YouTube Theater, 8:49 pm.</figcaption></figure>

  <h3 id="wcs-2022">We Can Survive again · Hollywood Bowl · October 22, 2022</h3>
  <p>
    A year after the first one, we went back to the Bowl for <em>We Can Survive</em> 2022. The lineup was OneRepublic,
    Halsey, Weezer, Alanis Morissette and Garbage. Inside the shell stood a wide, curved video wall, and at the
    end of the set it said <strong>WE CAN SURVIVE</strong> under the Audacy logo, on a starry blue background. The
    phone recorded OneRepublic's set from 7:28 to 8:06: a big group with keyboards, horns and drums, in front of
    screens that kept changing, from forests to a close-up of a face in sunglasses.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'wcs-2022-screen.webp'} alt="A band on the Hollywood Bowl stage in front of a wide blue video wall reading Audacy and WE CAN SURVIVE." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The Bowl's video wall, 8:05 pm.</figcaption></figure>

  <h3 id="kroq-2022">KROQ Almost Acoustic Christmas · Kia Forum · December 10, 2022</h3>
  <p>
    Back at the Forum in December, for the Los Angeles rock station KROQ's annual holiday show, <em>Almost Acoustic
    Christmas</em>. The photos start late, a little before eleven, with a group holding microphones on stage in
    front of a tartan screen that read <strong>KROQ Almost Acoustic Christmas</strong>. The set that followed, the
    last of the night, was Imagine Dragons again, three months after the stadium. The videos show the same singer in a white tank top,
    the same long-haired guitarist, tall portrait screens on either side of the drums, and the lights going
    orange and red as the set went on. Måneskin, from that January, were on the same bill.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'kroq-screen.webp'} alt="A tartan-patterned screen reading KROQ Almost Acoustic Christmas behind a group of people on stage, in blue light." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Between sets, 10:49 pm.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'kroq-stage.webp'} alt="A band on a dark blue stage with two tall portrait screens showing a long-haired guitarist, and white beams of light." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The last set of the night, 11:40 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2>2023</h2>

  <h3 id="eras-2023">Taylor Swift, The Eras Tour · SoFi Stadium · August 3, 2023</h3>
  <p>
    The biggest night in the collection, and probably the hardest ticket. <em>The Eras Tour</em> went on to be the
    highest-grossing concert tour of all time, and Los Angeles got six nights at <strong>SoFi Stadium</strong>, which
    opened in 2020 as home to the Rams and the Chargers. Ours was the first of the six, on a Thursday. The stadium
    sat under a pink sunset as we walked in at ten to eight.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'eras-sofi.webp'} alt="SoFi Stadium's long, low, curved roof in the distance at sunset, beyond palm trees and an empty plaza, with a plane in the sky." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>SoFi Stadium at sunset, 7:49 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    The show runs more than three hours and goes through her albums one "era" at a time, with new sets and costumes
    for each. At 8:23 she was out on the far end of the long runway, in a sparkling bodysuit and silver boots, with
    the stands behind her full of colored lights. At 8:40 the giant screen showed her with a pink guitar, arms
    stretched wide, next to a doll's house with every room lit in a different color, the set for the
    <em>Lover</em> section. The videos go on until nearly midnight: columns of white smoke, dancers in orange,
    and, near the end, big purple clouds carried across the stage.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'eras-b-stage.webp'} alt="Taylor Swift in a sparkling bodysuit and silver boots singing at the end of a raised runway, with tiers of stadium seats full of lights behind her." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The end of the runway, 8:23 pm.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'eras-lover-house.webp'} alt="A giant stadium screen showing Taylor Swift with a pink guitar and arms outstretched, next to a lit doll's house with colored rooms." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The <em>Lover</em> house, 8:40 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    At 10:22 she was on the screen in a long cream dress, next to a cabin with a moss-covered roof and a smoking
    chimney under blue trees: the set for <em>folklore</em>.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'eras-folklore.webp'} alt="Taylor Swift in a long cream dress on a giant blue screen, next to a cabin with a moss-covered roof and a smoking chimney on the stage." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The <em>folklore</em> cabin, 10:22 pm.</figcaption></figure>

  <h3>Adele and KÀ · Las Vegas · September 2–3, 2023</h3>
  <p>
    Labor Day weekend was a trip built around a ticket. On the Saturday we saw Adele's residency, <em>Weekends with
    Adele</em>, at the Colosseum at Caesars Palace: a nearly bare stage, a white piano and two tall beams of green
    light. On the Sunday we saw <em>KÀ</em>, Cirque du Soleil's show at the MGM Grand, where the stage is a huge deck
    on a robotic arm that tilts until it is almost vertical. Both are in
    <a href="/misc/labor-day-2023">Rainbows, Adele and Zzyzx</a>.
  </p>

  <h3 id="ed-sheeran-2023">Ed Sheeran, +–=÷× Tour · SoFi Stadium · September 23, 2023</h3>
  <p>
    Seven weeks after Taylor Swift we were back at SoFi. The stage was in the round, in the middle of the
    stadium: a ring of screens hung over it, showing hand-drawn clouds and flowers, and red masts
    wrapped in rings of light stood around it. After the show, from the upper deck, the empty floor showed the whole
    design: the round stage, the masts, and screens shaped like giant guitar picks.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'ed-sheeran-stage.webp'} alt="A round stage in the middle of a stadium under a hanging ring of screens with hand-drawn clouds and flowers, surrounded by red masts wrapped in rings of light." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The stage in the round, 9:10 pm.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'ed-sheeran-after.webp'} alt="The stadium floor from the upper deck after the show: the round stage, red masts and guitar-pick-shaped screens, with crew in yellow vests clearing it." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>After the show, 10:57 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h3 id="genshin-2023">Genshin Concert · Peacock Theater · November 19, 2023</h3>
  <p>
    A game concert. <em>Genshin Concert 2023: Melodies of an Endless Journey</em> was a symphony tour of the music
    from Genshin Impact, a game I play.
    It came to the <strong>Peacock Theater</strong> at L.A. Live, the 7,100-seat theater that opened in 2007 as the
    Nokia Theatre and hosts the Emmys. A full orchestra, harp on the left, played under a big screen showing
    footage from the game: green valleys and windmills for the first region, Mondstadt, and later lanterns rising
    over a city at night, storms, battles and the characters. Between pieces the screen went back to the title.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'genshin-orchestra.webp'} alt="An orchestra with a golden harp on a dark stage, under a large screen showing a green valley with a windmill from the game Genshin Impact." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The orchestra under the game, 7:31 pm.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'genshin-title.webp'} alt="A large screen reading Genshin Concert, Melodies of an Endless Journey, above an orchestra on stage." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The title screen, 8:04 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    The audience was part of the show too. Some people came in costume as their favorite characters, which you
    don't see at most orchestra concerts. After the concert, many fans in costume posed together on the plaza outside
    for a photo.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'genshin-lanterns.webp'} alt="An orchestra and its conductor on a dark stage under a large screen showing lanterns rising over a city at night from the game." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Lanterns on the screen, 8:08 pm.</figcaption></figure>

  <h2>2024</h2>

  <h3><em>O</em> · Bellagio, Las Vegas · June 2024</h3>
  <p>
    In June 2024 I took my parents to Las Vegas, and the trip was mostly shows. We saw <em>O</em>, Cirque du Soleil's
    water show at the Bellagio, where the stage is a pool and the floor seems to turn from water to solid ground and
    back. We also went inside the Sphere for <em>Postcard from Earth</em>, a film made for the venue. My wife and my
    parents also saw David Copperfield, two years after I had. That trip is section 5 of
    <a href="/misc/las-vegas">Las Vegas, Again</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2025</h2>

  <h3>Kenshi Yonezu · YouTube Theater · April 6, 2025</h3>
  <p>
    The one show in this collection with nothing to show. Kenshi Yonezu is one of the biggest names in Japanese pop,
    known outside Japan for "Lemon" and for theme songs to anime such as <em>Chainsaw Man</em>. In April 2025 he
    played the YouTube Theater, and we were there. Photography and video were not allowed, so there are no
    photos of the show, and this section has to do without one.
  </p>

  <h3><em>Mad Apple</em> and Bruno Mars · Las Vegas · August 30–31, 2025</h3>
  <p>
    Labor Day weekend in Las Vegas again, this time with our dog. On the Saturday we saw <em>Mad Apple</em>, Cirque du
    Soleil's show at New York-New York, a love letter to New York told with acrobatics, comedy and music. On the
    Sunday night we saw <strong>Bruno Mars</strong> at Dolby Live in Park MGM, the theater where he plays his Las Vegas
    residency. There are no photos from inside that show. The photos from that night are of Bruno Mars ads on the
    Strip and, back in the room, the merch: two T-shirts and a button pack. Both nights are in section 6 of
    <a href="/misc/las-vegas">Las Vegas, Again</a>.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'mad-apple-bows.webp'} alt="The full cast of Mad Apple taking bows on a purple-lit round stage, with a yellow taxi, shelves of bottles and a band platform behind them." loading="lazy" /><figcaption><em>Mad Apple</em>'s curtain call, 8:32 pm, August 30th.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'bruno-nyny.webp'} alt="The New York-New York sign at night above a tall blue screen reading Bruno Mars, This Week, Dolby Live at Park MGM, with palm trees below." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Bruno Mars on the New York-New York tower, 11:43 pm, August 31st.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h3 id="david-tao-2025">David Tao, Soul Power II · Kia Forum · December 20, 2025</h3>
  <p>
    The fourth and last night at the Forum, and the first concert in the collection sung mostly in Mandarin. David
    Tao (陶喆) is the Taiwanese singer-songwriter who, in the late 1990s, brought R&amp;B into Mandopop, and a lot
    of people who grew up with Chinese pop music know his songs by heart. His <em>Soul Power II</em> tour came to
    Inglewood on a Saturday night. The Forum was lit pink again, as it was for Måneskin four years earlier, and this
    time the letters on the colonnade read DAVID TAO.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'tao-forum.webp'} alt="The round, colonnaded Kia Forum lit pink at night across a wide empty parking lot, with KIA FORUM in white letters on top." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The Forum, 7:59 pm.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'tao-stage.webp'} alt="The inside of the Kia Forum with a stage at the far end and screens reading SOUL POWER on both sides of a blue graffiti-style Los Angeles logo, under red lights." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>SOUL POWER and "Los Angeles" on the screens, 8:14 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    Inside, the screens on either side of the stage said <strong>SOUL POWER</strong>, with "Los Angeles" scrawled
    between them in blue graffiti letters. The audience had light sticks with the tour name printed on them, and at
    times the whole floor turned red. At 9:53 pm David Tao was singing at a keyboard, large on the screen beside the
    stage, with his band on the stage and the light sticks glowing white below.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'tao-on-stage.webp'} alt="David Tao singing at a keyboard, shown large on a screen beside a dark stage where his band plays under a spotlight beam, and a floor full of small lights below." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>David Tao on stage, 9:53 pm.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'tao-light-stick.webp'} alt="A light stick glowing white with DAVID TAO and SOUL POWER II printed on it, in front of a dark arena full of small lights." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The <em>Soul Power II</em> light stick, 9:53 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2>2026</h2>

  <h3 id="lang-lang-2026">Lang Lang plays Beethoven · Segerstrom Concert Hall · March 23, 2026</h3>
  <p>
    The one evening of classical music in this post, down in Orange County: <strong>Renée and Henry
    Segerstrom Concert Hall</strong> in Costa Mesa, home of the Pacific Symphony. The hall opened in 2006, and
    inside it is all curving cream balconies stacked around a wooden stage, with organ pipes behind. The
    screen over the stage said it simply: <strong>March 23 · Lang Lang Plays Beethoven</strong>. Lang Lang is
    probably the most famous classical pianist in the world. He played at the opening ceremony of the 2008 Beijing
    Olympics. With Carl St.Clair conducting, the Pacific Symphony opened with Beethoven's <em>Egmont</em>
    Overture and Dvořák's "New World" Symphony, and Lang Lang came on after the intermission for Beethoven's Third
    Piano Concerto.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'lang-lang-screen.webp'} alt="A concert hall with curving cream balconies around a stage, an orchestra on stage and a screen reading March 23, Lang Lang Plays Beethoven, Pacific Symphony." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Before the concert, 8:03 pm.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'lang-lang-piano.webp'} alt="The same hall with a grand piano at the center of the stage among the orchestra, and the screen above showing a close-up of the musicians." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The piano in place, 9:24 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    The first photo, at 8:03, shows only the orchestra. By 9:24, after the intermission, a black grand piano had
    been rolled to the middle of the stage. The last two videos, just after ten, are of the end: the whole hall on its feet, the orchestra
    standing, and Lang Lang on the screen taking his bows.
  </p>

  <h3 id="bruno-sofi-2026">Bruno Mars, The Romantic Tour · SoFi Stadium · October 6, 2026</h3>
  <p>
    And back to SoFi, three years after the Eras Tour, for Bruno Mars a second time. Thirteen months after the
    Dolby Live theater in Las Vegas, this was the stadium version: <em>The Romantic Tour</em>. The name was
    written over the stage in big orange letters, and the stage was a wall of lights. The videos run from before nine to
    almost eleven. They show Bruno Mars in a headband and a light-blue jacket, the band in matching outfits on the
    side screens, horns, fireworks, and a mirror ball glittering in the smoke.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'bruno-sofi.webp'} alt="A stadium stage glowing orange with a wall of lights and THE ROMANTIC in large letters at the center, flanked by screens showing two singers in front of microphones." loading="lazy" /><figcaption><em>The Romantic</em> at SoFi Stadium, 10:54 pm.</figcaption></figure>

  <h2>Five years, from the floor</h2>
  <p>
    Put together, the five years look like this: a lot of the Kia Forum, a lot of Inglewood in general, two
    radio-station nights at the Bowl, and a weekend in Las Vegas whenever there was a show we really wanted to see.
    It also shows something I hadn't noticed. Very few of these were big plans. Some of the tickets were bought
    only a day or two before, because someone we liked happened to be in town.
  </p>
  <p>
    Going through the videos, I also noticed how little of the music is in them. The phone hears a stadium as a
    wall of noise. What the clips keep is everything around the music: the wristbands at the Bowl, the confetti, the
    light sticks at the Forum, the moment a hall stands up. The one night with no video at all, Kenshi Yonezu, is
    not any harder to remember than the others. Maybe there is a lesson in that, but I will probably still take my
    phone out next time.
  </p>
